  "lead_raw_text": " The structure of Eu2Pm2O7 (EuPmO3.5) crystallizes in the monoclinic space group C2/c (No. 15), with a unit cell of 32 atoms (Eu8Pm8O28) distributed over six independent Wyckoff orbits. Geometry-derived analysis identifies octahedral Eu centers coordinated by six O neighbors (Eu–O distances 2.27–2.51 Å) and octahedral Pm centers coordinated by six O neighbors (2.24–2.43 Å). Oxygen environments include square-pyramidal motifs with two Eu and three Pm neighbors, plus additional 4- and 5-coordinate O sites. Validated polyhedron-sharing relations show corner- and edge-sharing between Eu and Pm octahedra, and edge-sharing among square-pyramidal O polyhedra, forming a single 3-periodic connectivity component spanning all 32 sites.\n<CRYSTAL_START>",
